      "id": "6d95eafb-5ed5-4c45-b144-ffabd4d21566",
      "name": "Route and deduplicate",
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Persistent notification state belongs to the local serialized router, not\n// n8n's per-execution static-data snapshots.\nconst alerts = $input.all().flatMap(({json}) => {\n  const raw = json.body ?? json;\n  return json.body || raw.title !== undefined || raw.source !== undefined ? [raw] : [];\n});\nconst result = await this.helpers.httpRequest({method: 'POST',\n  url: $env.ALERT_ROUTER_URL, body: alerts, json: true, timeout: 30000});\nreturn [{json: result}];\n"
      },
      "position": [
        220,
        180
      ],
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "59efa63e-de67-447c-9035-cee11e957a8b",
      "name": "Usage",
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "content": "## Notification policy\n\nThe local notification router persists and serializes the queue. Ordinary alerts wait from 22:00 to 07:00 Europe/Berlin. Critical problems bypass quiet hours. Open problems repeat daily and send a recovery notice. Set event: true for a one-off notification such as a new media request or timetable change.",
